IMPORT prelude

-- Virginia Temporary Assistance for Needy Families (TANF), Code of Virginia Title 63.2, chapter 6, with the Board's income rules
-- (22VAC40-295-10, -50) brought in -- what a family meets: who is an eligible child (s 63.2-602 A, 22VAC40-295-10 "child"),
-- what the applicant must do (s 63.2-602 B), the immunization reduction (s 63.2-603), income eligibility, the disregards and the
-- monthly payment (22VAC40-295-50 A, B 10, B 15, B 23, C, D, I), VIEW exemptions (s 63.2-609), the 24-month limit and the
-- 60-day notice before termination (s 63.2-612), diversionary cash assistance (s 63.2-617 A) and continued payment on appeal
-- (s 63.2-618).
--
-- SEAT: the caretaker (parent or relative) applying for or receiving TANF for a child ("Is my child eligible? Are we income
-- eligible, and how much will we get? Must I take part in VIEW? When does the 24 months end, and must I be told? What is
-- diversionary assistance worth? Do payments continue if I appeal?"). Provisions addressed to the local department are encoded
-- as what they mean for that person.
--
-- Edition: the Code of Virginia as online after the 2026 Session (Virginia Law Portal), retrieved 2026-10-19 (UTC), as deposited
-- at ../../registers/source-bundle/title-63-2-chapter-6-temporary-assistance-for-needy-families.txt; and 22VAC40-295-10 and -50
-- as shown online on 10/19/2026, deposited in the sibling subject
-- ../../../virginia-administrative-code-22vac40-295-tanf-income-and-payment/registers/source-bundle/va-22vac40-295-10-50-tanf.txt.
--
-- AMOUNTS NOT DEPOSITED. The standard of assistance by family size ("established by the State Board of Social Services",
-- 22VAC40-295-10), the SNAP standard deduction used in the earned income disregard (22VAC40-295-50 C 1; set under the federal
-- Food and Nutrition Act, whose annual tables are deposited in subjects/us/food-and-nutrition-act-of-2008) and the percentage of
-- the poverty level in s 63.2-614 C 1 are INPUTS.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Funding (ss 63.2-601.1, 601.2); VIEW activities and case management (ss 63.2-608, 610, 611) except exemptions;
-- s 63.2-605 (vendor payments after a failed drug test); s 63.2-607 (minor parents; asked only as a fact through eligibility);
-- s 63.2-613 hardship exceptions (Board regulations not deposited: asked as a fact); s 63.2-614 A step-parent deeming and C 1
-- (the VIEW earned income cap, an input); s 63.2-617 B emergency assistance; s 63.2-621; the other disregards of
-- 22VAC40-295-50 B (the person leaves disregarded income out of the income they state).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Virginia TANF -- Code of Virginia ss 63.2-600 to 63.2-621, 22VAC40-295-10 and -50`

§§ `The parties and the actions`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the caretaker`
    `the local department`

DECLARE `Action` IS ONE OF
    `give written notice that TANF is scheduled to end`
    `request a hearing`
    `continue direct payment of TANF pending the appeal`

§§ `s 63.2-602 -- an eligible child`

-- s 63.2-602 A: "A person shall be eligible ... if that person: 1. Has not attained the age of 18 years, or, if a full-time
-- student in a secondary school or in the equivalent level of career and technical education, has not attained the age of
-- nineteen years; 2. Is a resident of Virginia; 3. Is living with his father, mother, grandfather, grandmother, brother, sister,
-- stepfather, stepmother, stepbrother, stepsister, uncle, aunt, first cousin, nephew, or niece in a residence maintained by such
-- relative or is in placement under conditions specified by the Board; 4. Is in need of public assistance; and 5. If less than
-- 18 years of age, is in compliance with compulsory school attendance laws". "In need" is read through the income test of
-- 22VAC40-295-50 A (a separate question).
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
      `full-time in secondary school or equivalent career and technical education` IS A BOOLEAN
      `resident of Virginia` IS A BOOLEAN
      `lives with a listed relative in a home the relative maintains, or in a Board placement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in compliance with compulsory school attendance laws` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the s 63.2-602 A conditions other than need` IF
        (`age` LESS THAN 18 OR (`full-time in secondary school or equivalent career and technical education` AND `age` LESS THAN 19))
    AND `resident of Virginia`
    AND `lives with a listed relative in a home the relative maintains, or in a Board placement`
    AND (`age` AT LEAST 18 OR `in compliance with compulsory school attendance laws`)

-- s 63.2-602 B: the applicant "shall: 1. Furnish, apply for or have an application made ... for a social security account
-- number ...; 2. Assign the Commonwealth any rights to support ...; 3. Identify the parents of the child ... subject to the
-- 'good cause' provisions ... [not where] the child is in a foster care placement or ... was conceived as the result of incest or
-- rape; and 4. Cooperate in ... locating the parent ..., establishing the paternity ..., obtaining support payments". These are
-- conditions of the application, with no deadline in the text.
GIVEN `I have furnished or applied for social security numbers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have assigned my support rights to the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have identified the parents, or an exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I cooperate with child support enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant meets s 63.2-602 B` IF
        `I have furnished or applied for social security numbers`
    AND `I have assigned my support rights to the Commonwealth`
    AND `I have identified the parents, or an exception applies`
    AND `I cooperate with child support enforcement`

§§ `s 63.2-603 -- immunizations`

-- s 63.2-603: "Failure by the recipient to provide the required verification of immunizations shall result in a reduction in the
-- amount of monthly assistance ... The reduction shall be $50 for the first child and $25 for each additional child for whom
-- verification is not provided." "No sanction may be imposed until the reason for the failure ... has been identified and any
-- barriers to accessing immunizations have been removed."
GIVEN `children without verification` IS A NUMBER
      `the reason is identified and barriers removed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the immunization reduction` `children without verification` `the reason is identified and barriers removed` MEANS
    IF `children without verification` LESS THAN 1 OR NOT (`the reason is identified and barriers removed`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE 50 PLUS (25 TIMES (`children without verification` MINUS 1))

§§ `22VAC40-295-50 -- income eligibility and the payment`

-- 22VAC40-295-50 C: "When determining initial eligibility, or ongoing eligibility for non-VIEW participants, the following is
-- disregarded from the monthly earned income of the assistance unit: 1. An amount equal to the standard deduction used in the
-- Food Stamp program; and 2. Twenty percent of the remainder." D: "The earned income of a student, who is not the head of
-- household, under 18 years of age shall be disregarded" (the person leaves it out). B 23: "The first $50 of total child or
-- spousal support payments received each month". B 10: "Any portion of an SSI payment"; B 15: "Income tax refunds including
-- earned income tax credit advance payments and refunds" (left out).
GIVEN `monthly earned income` IS A NUMBER
      `SNAP standard deduction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the countable earned income` `monthly earned income` `SNAP standard deduction` MEANS
    (max 0 (`monthly earned income` MINUS `SNAP standard deduction`)) TIMES 80%

GIVEN `monthly earned income` IS A NUMBER
      `SNAP standard deduction` IS A NUMBER
      `monthly child or spousal support` IS A NUMBER
      `other monthly unearned income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the net income` `monthly earned income` `SNAP standard deduction` `monthly child or spousal support` `other monthly unearned income` MEANS
    sum (LIST `the countable earned income` `monthly earned income` `SNAP standard deduction`,
              max 0 (`monthly child or spousal support` MINUS 50),
              `other monthly unearned income`)

-- 22VAC40-295-50 A: "The assistance unit is income eligible if the net income of the assistance unit is less than the standard
-- of assistance." I: "The monthly payment amount is equal to the standard of assistance minus the net income."
DECLARE `Payment outcome` IS ONE OF
    `not income eligible: net income is not less than the standard of assistance (22VAC40-295-50 A)`
    `a monthly payment of` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `standard of assistance` IS A NUMBER
      `net income` IS A NUMBER
      `immunization reduction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Payment outcome`
`the monthly payment` `standard of assistance` `net income` `immunization reduction` MEANS
    IF `net income` LESS THAN `standard of assistance`
    THEN `a monthly payment of` (max 0 ((`standard of assistance` MINUS `net income`) MINUS `immunization reduction`))
    ELSE `not income eligible: net income is not less than the standard of assistance (22VAC40-295-50 A)`

§§ `s 63.2-609 -- VIEW exemptions`

-- s 63.2-609: exempt from mandatory VIEW participation: "1. Any individual ... under 16 years of age; 2. Any individual at least
-- 16, but no more than 19 years of age, who is enrolled full time in elementary or secondary school ...; 3. ... enrolled full
-- time in an accredited public institution of higher education ... [leading] to a postsecondary credential [to the extent federal
-- law allows]; 4. ... unable to participate because of a temporary medical condition ... certified by a written medical
-- statement ...; 5. Any individual who is disabled, as determined by receipt of Social Security Disability Benefits or
-- Supplemental Security Income; 6. Any individual 60 years of age or older; 7. ... the sole caregiver of another member of the
-- household who is disabled ... and whose presence is essential ...; or 8. A parent or caretaker-relative of a child under 12
-- months of age who personally provides care for the child ... for a period of no more than 12 months."
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
      `full time in elementary or secondary school` IS A BOOLEAN
      `full time in an accredited postsecondary credential programme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certified temporary medical condition prevents work or training` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I receive SSDI or SSI` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am the sole essential caregiver of a disabled household member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I personally care for my child under 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `months already exempt for caring for an infant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is exempt from VIEW` IF
       `age` LESS THAN 16
    OR (`age` AT LEAST 16 AND `age` AT MOST 19 AND `full time in elementary or secondary school`)
    OR `full time in an accredited postsecondary credential programme`
    OR `a certified temporary medical condition prevents work or training`
    OR `I receive SSDI or SSI`
    OR `age` AT LEAST 60
    OR `I am the sole essential caregiver of a disabled household member`
    OR (`I personally care for my child under 12 months` AND `months already exempt for caring for an infant` LESS THAN 12)

§§ `s 63.2-612 -- the 24 months`

DECLARE `Time limit outcome` IS ONE OF
    `exempt from VIEW: the 24-month limit does not apply to me (s 63.2-612 "Unless otherwise exempt")`
    `within the 24 months`
    `past 24 months, but a hardship exception applies (s 63.2-613)`
    `a relative with whom a child was placed after a child protective services report: eligible at once (s 63.2-612)`
    `past 24 months: not eligible until 24 further months have passed`
    `eligible again after the 24-month period of ineligibility`

-- s 63.2-612: "Unless otherwise exempt, VIEW participants and their families may receive TANF financial assistance for a maximum
-- of 24 months only, subject to s 63.2-613. VIEW participants and their families may receive TANF financial assistance, if
-- otherwise eligible, after a subsequent period of 24 months. However, the 24-month period of ineligibility shall not apply when a
-- child is removed from the parents' home as the result of a child protective services report ... and is placed with a relative."
GIVEN `exempt from VIEW` IS A BOOLEAN
      `months of TANF received as a VIEW participant` IS A NUMBER
      `a hardship exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a relative with whom a child was placed after a CPS report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `months since the 24 months ended` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Time limit outcome`
`the 24-month limit` `exempt from VIEW` `months of TANF received as a VIEW participant` `a hardship exception applies` `I am a relative with whom a child was placed after a CPS report` `months since the 24 months ended` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `exempt from VIEW` THEN `exempt from VIEW: the 24-month limit does not apply to me (s 63.2-612 "Unless otherwise exempt")`
        IF `months of TANF received as a VIEW participant` LESS THAN 24 THEN `within the 24 months`
        IF `a hardship exception applies` THEN `past 24 months, but a hardship exception applies (s 63.2-613)`
        IF `I am a relative with whom a child was placed after a CPS report` THEN `a relative with whom a child was placed after a child protective services report: eligible at once (s 63.2-612)`
        IF `months since the 24 months ended` AT LEAST 24 THEN `eligible again after the 24-month period of ineligibility`
        OTHERWISE `past 24 months: not eligible until 24 further months have passed`

-- s 63.2-612: "The local department shall notify a VIEW participant and his family that his TANF financial assistance is
-- scheduled to be terminated ... Notice shall be given 60 days prior to such termination". What the caretaker must be given:
-- counted in days from the start of the last 24-month period's final stretch, the notice is due by the 60th day before the
-- scheduled termination.
GIVEN `days until the scheduled termination` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Action`
`the notice I must be given before TANF ends` `days until the scheduled termination` MEANS
    PARTY  `the local department`
    MUST   `give written notice that TANF is scheduled to end`
    WITHIN max 0 (`days until the scheduled termination` MINUS 60)
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the local department` BECAUSE "no notice 60 days before the scheduled termination of TANF (Va. Code s 63.2-612)"

§§ `s 63.2-617 A -- diversionary cash assistance`

-- s 63.2-617 A: "the maximum TANF cash assistance that the applicant would otherwise receive for a period up to 120 days or
-- $1,500, whichever is greater. An individual may receive diversionary TANF cash assistance only one time in a 12-month period
-- and, in so doing, waives his eligibility for TANF for the number of days for which assistance is granted multiplied by 1.33."
-- The 120 days are taken as four months of the monthly payment (NOTES.md finding 4).
GIVEN `monthly TANF payment I would otherwise receive` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most diversionary assistance can be` `monthly TANF payment I would otherwise receive` MEANS
    max (`monthly TANF payment I would otherwise receive` TIMES 4) 1500

GIVEN `days for which assistance is granted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days of TANF eligibility waived` `days for which assistance is granted` MEANS
    `days for which assistance is granted` TIMES 1.33

§§ `s 63.2-618 -- appeal`

-- s 63.2-618: "If a hearing request is received prior to the effective date of any proposed change in benefit status, a
-- participant appealing such change shall have the right to continued direct payment of TANF benefits pending final
-- administrative action". The request is the participant's choice (DO ... LEST FULFILLED; a MAY would fire HENCE when unused).
GIVEN `days from the notice to the effective date of the change` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Action`
`my appeal of a change in benefits` `days from the notice to the effective date of the change` MEANS
    PARTY  `the caretaker`
    DO     `request a hearing`
    WITHIN `days from the notice to the effective date of the change`
    HENCE  `payment continues pending the appeal`
    LEST   FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Action`
`payment continues pending the appeal` MEANS
    PARTY  `the local department`
    MUST   `continue direct payment of TANF pending the appeal`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the local department` BECAUSE "TANF stopped although the hearing request came before the effective date (Va. Code s 63.2-618)"

§ `Questions for the caretaker`

§§ `Is my child eligible?`

@export Does my child meet Virginia's TANF eligibility conditions other than need (Va. Code s 63.2-602 A)?
GIVEN `my child's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The child's age in whole years
      `my child is a full-time secondary or equivalent career and technical student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child is a full-time student in secondary school or the equivalent level of career and technical education
      `my child lives in Virginia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child is a resident of Virginia
      `my child lives with a listed relative in a home that relative keeps` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child lives with a father, mother, grandparent, brother, sister, step-parent, step-sibling, uncle, aunt, first cousin, nephew or niece in a home that relative maintains, or is in a placement on the Board's conditions
      `my child is in compliance with school attendance laws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a child under 18: whether the child is complying with the compulsory school attendance laws
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my child meet the TANF conditions` IF
    `meets the s 63.2-602 A conditions other than need` `my child's age` `my child is a full-time secondary or equivalent career and technical student` `my child lives in Virginia` `my child lives with a listed relative in a home that relative keeps` `my child is in compliance with school attendance laws`

@export Have I done what Virginia requires of a TANF applicant (Va. Code s 63.2-602 B)?
GIVEN `I have given or applied for social security numbers for everyone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have furnished, or applied for, a social security number for yourself and every child you are applying for
      `I have assigned support rights to the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have assigned to Virginia your rights to child or spousal support for the family members you apply for
      `I have identified the children's parents, or an exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have identified the parents of the child, or good cause, foster care placement, or conception by rape or incest excuses it
      `I am cooperating with child support enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you cooperate in locating the absent parent, establishing paternity and obtaining support
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I met the applicant requirements` IF
    `the applicant meets s 63.2-602 B` `I have given or applied for social security numbers for everyone` `I have assigned support rights to the Commonwealth` `I have identified the children's parents, or an exception applies` `I am cooperating with child support enforcement`

§§ `How much will we get?`

@export Are we income eligible for Virginia TANF, and what is our monthly payment (22VAC40-295-50; Va. Code s 63.2-603)?
GIVEN `our standard of assistance` IS A NUMBER @desc The monthly standard of assistance the State Board of Social Services sets for your family size, in US dollars (not in the deposited text)
      `our monthly earned income` IS A NUMBER @desc The family's monthly wages, salary, commissions or self-employment profit, in US dollars; leave out earnings of a student under 18 who is not head of household
      `the SNAP standard deduction` IS A NUMBER @desc The monthly standard deduction used in the SNAP (Food Stamp) program for your household size, in US dollars
      `our monthly child or spousal support` IS A NUMBER @desc Child or spousal support the family receives each month, in US dollars
      `our other monthly unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc Other countable unearned income each month, in US dollars; leave out SSI, tax refunds and EITC, food benefits, housing subsidies, loans, and the other income 22VAC40-295-50 B disregards
      `children without immunization verification` IS A NUMBER @desc How many children not in school or licensed child care lack the required verification of immunizations
      `the reason has been identified and barriers removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local department has identified why verification is missing and removed any barriers to immunization
GIVETH A `Payment outcome`
`What is our Virginia TANF payment` `our standard of assistance` `our monthly earned income` `the SNAP standard deduction` `our monthly child or spousal support` `our other monthly unearned income` `children without immunization verification` `the reason has been identified and barriers removed` MEANS
    `the monthly payment` `our standard of assistance` (`the net income` `our monthly earned income` `the SNAP standard deduction` `our monthly child or spousal support` `our other monthly unearned income`) (`the immunization reduction` `children without immunization verification` `the reason has been identified and barriers removed`)

@export At most how much diversionary cash assistance can I get at once, and how many days of TANF eligibility would I waive (Va. Code s 63.2-617 A)?
GIVEN `the monthly TANF payment I would otherwise get` IS A NUMBER @desc The monthly TANF payment you would otherwise receive, in US dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`At most how much diversionary assistance can I get` `the monthly TANF payment I would otherwise get` MEANS
    `the most diversionary assistance can be` `the monthly TANF payment I would otherwise get`

@export For how many days would I waive TANF eligibility if granted diversionary assistance (Va. Code s 63.2-617 A)?
GIVEN `the days the assistance covers` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days for which diversionary assistance is granted
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many days of TANF eligibility would I waive` `the days the assistance covers` MEANS
    `the days of TANF eligibility waived` `the days the assistance covers`

§§ `Must I take part in VIEW, and when do the 24 months end?`

@export Am I exempt from taking part in VIEW, Virginia's TANF work programme (Va. Code s 63.2-609)?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `I am in elementary or secondary school full time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are enrolled full time in elementary or secondary school (or equivalent career and technical education)
      `I am in an accredited postsecondary credential programme full time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are enrolled full time in an accredited public institution of higher education or licensed postsecondary school on a course leading to a credential
      `a certified temporary medical condition stops me working or training` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a physician or other qualified medical professional has certified in writing a temporary medical condition preventing employment or training (reviewed every 60 days)
      `I receive SSDI or SSI` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive Social Security Disability benefits or Supplemental Security Income
      `I am the sole caregiver essential to a disabled household member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the sole caregiver of a disabled or incapacitated household member and your presence is essential to their care
      `I personally care for my baby under 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a parent or caretaker-relative personally caring for a child under 12 months
      `months I have already been exempt for an infant` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months (consecutive or not) you have already been exempt for caring for a child under 12 months
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I exempt from VIEW` IF
    `is exempt from VIEW` `my age` `I am in elementary or secondary school full time` `I am in an accredited postsecondary credential programme full time` `a certified temporary medical condition stops me working or training` `I receive SSDI or SSI` `I am the sole caregiver essential to a disabled household member` `I personally care for my baby under 12 months` `months I have already been exempt for an infant`

@export Can my family still receive TANF under Virginia's 24-month limit (Va. Code ss 63.2-612, 63.2-613)?
GIVEN `I am exempt from VIEW` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are exempt from mandatory VIEW participation
      `months of TANF received while in VIEW` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months your family has received TANF while you were a VIEW participant, in the current period
      `a hardship exception has been granted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local department has granted you a hardship exception under the Board's regulations
      `I am a relative a child was placed with after a CPS report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a relative with whom a child was placed after being removed from the parents' home because of a child protective services report or complaint
      `months since our 24 months ended` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months have passed since your family's 24 months of TANF ended (0 if not ended)
GIVETH A `Time limit outcome`
`Can we still receive TANF under the 24-month limit` `I am exempt from VIEW` `months of TANF received while in VIEW` `a hardship exception has been granted` `I am a relative a child was placed with after a CPS report` `months since our 24 months ended` MEANS
    `the 24-month limit` `I am exempt from VIEW` `months of TANF received while in VIEW` `a hardship exception has been granted` `I am a relative a child was placed with after a CPS report` `months since our 24 months ended`

§§ `If our benefits are changed or stopped`

-- Situation: only where the local department has proposed to change or stop benefits.

@export If I ask for a hearing, does my TANF continue while the appeal is decided (Va. Code s 63.2-618)?
GIVEN `the day my hearing request is received` IS A NUMBER @desc The day the hearing request is received, counted in days from the notice of the proposed change
      `the day the change takes effect` IS A NUMBER @desc The day the proposed change in benefits takes effect, counted in days from the notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my TANF continue while I appeal` IF
    `the day my hearing request is received` LESS THAN `the day the change takes effect`
